{"uid":"bb4fbae927982756","name":"test_commit_scan_hold_is_never_released_by_a_ruling_even_on_a_signed_approach","fullName":"tests.test_commit_scan_escalation_digest#test_commit_scan_hold_is_never_released_by_a_ruling_even_on_a_signed_approach","historyId":"3d9c4c1141826fc8b6fe7ee68026b2fc","time":{"start":1791969240095,"stop":1791969240508,"duration":413},"description":"v0.36 D.1 (was cure-01-01-9): `resume_if_ruling_answers_pause` is gone,\n    so a ruling releases NO hold -- not even a commit-scan hold raised on an\n    approach that already carries a `rejectionSignatures` entry from an\n    earlier `operator_input_needed` park. This drives that history: a real\n    findings park (review's, task 014) lands first and is left by an ANSWER\n    (leaving `rejectionSignatures[\"1\"]` recorded and the run running again),\n    then a commit-scan hit parks a SECOND, unrelated hold on the SAME\n    approach. Its digest advertises `ralphctl unpause` alone, and a ruling\n    filed against it through the real CLI/engine route is recorded but the\n    run stays paused.","descriptionHtml":"<p>v0.36 D.1 (was cure-01-01-9): <code>resume_if_ruling_answers_pause</code> is gone,<br />\nso a ruling releases NO hold -- not even a commit-scan hold raised on an<br />\napproach that already carries a <code>rejectionSignatures</code> entry from an<br />\nearlier <code>operator_input_needed</code> park. This drives that history: a real<br />\nfindings park (review's, task 014) lands first and is left by an ANSWER<br />\n(leaving <code>rejectionSignatures[&quot;1&quot;]</code> recorded and the run running again),<br />\nthen a commit-scan hit parks a SECOND, unrelated hold on the SAME<br />\napproach. Its digest advertises <code>ralphctl unpause</code> alone, and a ruling<br />\nfiled against it through the real CLI/engine route is recorded but the<br />\nrun stays paused.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retries